From 6486e3dc0abd29c4d1ef0bc0845e82f0ea286cbd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 05:37:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 230/638] chrome: define native browser paths on AROS
 [chromium] [aros]

AI_PHASE: chromium-phase-4-browser-link

AI_STATUS: done

ROOT_CAUSE: Upstream Chrome had no AROS implementation for profile, cache, user-media, policy-variable, or initial-preferences paths, leaving the browser unable to establish filesystem identity.

FIX_REASON: Map durable browser state to ENVARC:Chromium, transient cache to T:Chromium, safe user-file defaults to RAM:, preserve profile access for AROS tasks, and resolve first-run/policy paths without Linux passwd or XDG assumptions.

SCOPE: New AROS Chrome path, first-run, and policy parser implementations plus their three GN registrations.

VALIDATION: All three new source files compiled; //chrome:chrome final linker inventory fell from 47 to 36 unresolved contracts; git diff --cached --check passes.

RISK: medium; assignment choices are native and writable on Live CD, but future multi-user AROS support may require a user-specific persistent profile assignment.

AI_DECISION_CHAIN: ACD-chromium-native-port-roadmap;
